alse, "num_turns": 16, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I found 11 rules whose behavior didn't match their docstrings, plus one that only read inconsistently, and fixed all 12 in `pricebook.py`. I then checked all 150 rules against a version built straight from each docstring, over a range of quantities and unit prices, and they all match now.\n\n| Problem | Rules | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Discount rounded with `round()` instead of floored to the won | 02, 45, 86 | `base * pct // 100` |\n| Threshold off by one (`qty > N` or `qty >= N+1`), so the discount started one unit late | 15, 30, 99, 116, 130, 139 | `qty >= N` |\n| Docstring says \"whole\", but the code discounted only the units above the threshold | 28, 125 | Discount the whole amount: `base * pct // 100` |\n| Condition was `qty >= 31` | 92 | `qty >= 30` |\n\nThe rule 92 change doesn't alter any prices: it's a \"marginal\" rule, so at exactly 30 units the discount is 0 either way. I changed it only so the code reads the same as the docstring.\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 2176, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 31902, "uuid": "52f2cdcc-3a67-4b5d-84a1-bb77a939892d", "ttft_stream_ms": 1552, "time_to_request_ms": 390, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 9, "system_prompt": 15, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 5, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 14, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 1, "message_prep": 1, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 1, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 327, "tool_schema_build": 6, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 2, "request_build": 2}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_to_request_loop_lag_ms": 2, "time_to_request_cpu_ms": 286, "time_to_request_major_faults": 0, "input_attachments_detail": {"slowest_producer": "model", "slowest_producer_ms": 3, "cpu_ms": 7, "major_faults": 0}, "first_content_frame_ms": 1553, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}